// What each argument of a command or environment is: text, typeset content, a dimension, keys, a name, a register,
// code. One table for every reader of a paper's source (the front end's arity, the layout maker's classes, the layer's
// source fallback): LaTeXML's prototypes (latexml-args.mjs, generated by scripts/latexml-args.mjs), with the commands
// below written out by hand where LaTeXML leaves an argument untyped, reads its arguments in code, or has no binding.
//
// A command's parameters are a string of pairs, shape then role:
